Everybody seems to agree that the ToM and the PYEC are the best
Quest artifacts in existence.  I was wondering whether this MMM
was the most useless.  From what I've heard so far, all this
gives you is a mirror, with some ESP and resistance to Magic Missiles.

Well, with all the nymphs in the game, I'm not short on mirrors.
ESP I could get from a Helm, or (what I usually do) I could run
around with a blindfold.  I think I've run out of non-telepathic
creatures that cause me any worry, so long as I take a peek
every now and then to have Excalibur notify me of traps.

The Magic Missile resistance is really not a boon.  Even before
I started the Quest I had a CoMR, AoR, and SoR.  Between the
three of those, I'm pretty safe against Magic Missiles, I'd say.

A glance thru the code indicates a SPEEK flag, but apparently
that isn't implemented to do anything.

Now, one thing that I'd really like to have from a Magic Mirror
is the 'Where's the Wiz' thing.  Anyone with their hands on mirror
code from before 3.1 would know what I mean by this.  I've asked
before for the telepathic mirror trick to be restored into
Nethack.  Maybe the MMM would allow you to do it without being blind.

If I don't find a good reason to hold onto the MMM,
I may just ditch it.  Anyone?

Roger Christman


